prose-a:text-[var(--color-action-blue-focus)] prose-img:rounded-xl"><h1 id=
=3D"chameleon-mini">Chameleon-Mini</h1>
<p>This is the official repository of ChameleonMini, a freely programmable,=
 portable tool for NFC security analysis that can emulate and clone contact=
less cards, read RFID tags and sniff/log RF data. Thanks to over 1700 backe=
rs from our <a href=3D"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1980078555/cham=
eleonmini-a-versatile-nfc-card-emulator-and-mo" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"no=
opener noreferrer" node=3D"[object Object]">Kickstarter project</a>, the cu=
rrent Revision G has been realized by Kasper &amp; Oswald GmbH.</p>
<p>The ChameleonMini RevG is now also available via the Kasper &amp; Oswald=
 <a href=3D"https://shop.kasper.it/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener nore=
ferrer" node=3D"[object Object]">Webshop</a>. Thank you for supporting the =
project!</p>
<h2 id=3D"important-third-party-clones">IMPORTANT: Third-party Clones</h2>
<p>We are aware of various third-party ChameleonMini clones or modified var=
iants that are available on the Internet. Warning: We have evidence that so=
me of these devices are defective or suffer from reading problems et cetera=
. Please understand that we cannot give support for these non-official devi=
ces, as we have no schematics / layout or other information, nor do we know=
 the manufacturers. In case of problems, please contact the manufacturers o=
f your device directly.</p>
<p>Note to the manufacturers: Some of the third-party ChameleonMini are vio=
lating the ChameleonMini license, please obey the license (see LICENSE.txt)=
!</p>
<h2 id=3D"first-steps">First Steps</h2>
<p>To upgrade the firmware of your ChameleonMini, please visit the <a href=
=3D"https://cdn.statically.io/gh/emsec/ChameleonMini/master/Doc/Doxygen/htm=
l/Page_GettingStarted.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" n=
ode=3D"[object Object]">Getting Started page</a> from the <a href=3D"https:=
//cdn.statically.io/gh/emsec/ChameleonMini/master/Doc/Doxygen/html/index.ht=
ml" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" node=3D"[object Object]">=
doxygen documentation</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"supported-cards-and-codecs">Supported Cards and Codecs</h2>
<p>See <a href=3D"https://github.com/emsec/ChameleonMini/wiki/Supported-Car=
ds-and--Codecs" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" node=3D"[obje=
ct Object]">here</a>. The linked wiki page also includes notes on DESFire e=
mulation and certain cases of application specific emulation (Gallagher).</=
p>
<h2 id=3D"questions">Questions</h2>
<p>If you have any questions, please visit the <a href=3D"https://github.co=
m/emsec/ChameleonMini/issues" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer"=
 node=3D"[object Object]">Issues page</a> and ask your questions there so e=
veryone benefits from the answer.</p>
<p><strong>Please note that we cannot give any support if you have issues w=
ith the RevE-rebooted hardware or any GUI. Please use this issues page only=
 for problems with the RevG hardware as distributed by Kasper &amp; Oswald =
and for problems with the firmware from this page.</strong></p>
<h2 id=3D"external-contributions">External Contributions</h2>
<p>We appreciate every contribution to the project. Have a look at the <a h=
ref=3D"https://github.com/emsec/ChameleonMini/wiki/External-Contributions" =
target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" node=3D"[object Object]">Exte=
rnal Contributions page</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"repository-structure">Repository Structure</h2>
<p>The code repository contains</p>
<ul>
<li>Doc: A doxygen documentation</li>
<li>Drivers: Chameleon drivers for Windows and Linux</li>
<li>Dumps: Dumps of different smartcards</li>
<li>Hardware: The layout and schematics of the PCB</li>
<li>Firmware: The complete firmware including a modified Atmel DFU bootload=
er and LUFA</li>
<li>Software: Contains a python tool for an easy configuration (and more) o=
f the ChameleonMini, Note that this is currently under construction</li>
<li>RevE: Contains the whole contents of the discontinued RevE repository.<=
/li>
<li>RevE-light: Contains our development files for the RevE-light - <strong=
>WARNING:</strong> currently not supported / not functional</li>
</ul></div></div></div></div></div><aside class=3D"space-y-6"><div class=3D=
